      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, we\u0027re using soft refs (JDK 21, generational ZGC, ~300 GB heap). Soft refs are kept until the heap is full and then cleared all at once, hot or cold, after threads have already stalled. We see `Major Collection (Allocation Stall)` evicting them several times a day.\n\nOur load is skewed. A few busy repos with large packs (.idx up to ~200 MB) should always stay resident, and the long tail touched by replication or an occasional fetch can go. A byte limit with LRU keeps the busy set and evicts the tail gradually, before the heap fills. Tuning `SoftRefLRUPolicyMSPerMB` doesn\u0027t help, since it is JVM-wide and only age-based.\n\nIt\u0027s the same reason JGit moved other caches off soft refs (WindowCache 709f83d48, RepositoryCache dea47b936, dfs.DeltaBaseCache 2eb16aa6c), and why DfsBlockCache already bounds index memory for DFS.",
      "parentUuid": "61173cec_19b7285d",
      "revId": "d97478898b4901b48474ce13b50e0115fdaeaab9",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
